  "Fly":"Fly to a target position",
  "Focused Conjuration":"Damage taken while you are Concentrating on a Conjuration spell will not break your Concentration.",
  "Fog Cloud":"Create a cloud of dense fog to Heavily Obscured and Blinded creatures within.",
  "Font of Inspiration":"You regain all of your Bardic Inspirations after a Long or Short Rest.",
  "Freedom of Movement":"Snap an ally out of any Stunned. Difficult Terrain can't slow them down, and they can't be magically Paralysed or Restrained. If the target is restrained by non-magical means, it can spend 1.5 m of Movement to free itself.",
  "Frenzy":"Your Rage turns into a frenzy! You gain Frenzied Strike and Enraged Throw. You can also make an Improvised Melee Weapon (Bonus Action) attack as a bonus action. Deal 2 extra damage with melee and improvised weapons, and throwing. Gain Resistance to physical damage, and Advantage on Strength Checks and Saving Throws.",
  "Fungal Infestation":"Raises a mildewed, mould-encrusted zombie from a corpse.",
  "Gaseous Form":"Transform yourself or an ally into a tiny gas cloud. It can't fall, and fits through small openings. It is very hard to damage. The cloud has Advantage on Constitution, Dexterity, and Strength Saving Throws.",
  "Giant's Rage":"Enter a Giant's Rage and increase in size. Your Rage damage bonus is doubled on Throw attacks. Gain Resistance to physical damage, and Advantage on Strength Checks and Saving Throws.",
  "Gong of the Summit":"Damages all nearby creatures and objects. Creatures made of inorganic material such as stone have Disadvantage on their Saving Throw.",
  "Grasping Vine":"Summon a giant vine capable of dragging creatures toward itself.",
  "Greater Invisibility":"Turn a creature Invisible. Attacks against it have Disadvantage. It attacks with Advantage. Invisibility breaks when you fail increasingly harder Stealth Checks on attacking, casting spells, or interacting with items.",
  "Greater Restoration":"Touch a creature and negate any Charm, Petrification, Stun, or Curse.",
  "Grim Harvest":"Once per turn, if you kill a creature with a spell, you regain Hit Points equal to twice the Spell Slot level used - thrice if it's a Necromancy spell. Undead and Constructs are unaffected.",
  "Guardian of Faith":"Call forth a divine guardian that attacks nearby enemies. Every time it deals damage, the guardian loses an equal amount of Hit Points.",
  "Guidance":"The target gains d4 +1d4 bonus to Checks.",
  "Guided Strike":"Gain a +10 bonus to your Attack Roll.",
  "Guiding Bolt":"The next attack roll against this target has Advantage.",
  "Gust of Wind":"Summon a strong wind that clears all clouds. Any creatures caught in the gale who fail a Strength Saving Throw will be pushed back 5 m and be thrown Off Balance.",
  "Halo of Spores":"Unleash a cloud of necrotic spores upon a target. This uses a reaction, so other reactions won't trigger this turn.",
  "Harmony of Fire and Water":"While not in combat, regain half of your Ki Points (rounded down).",
  "Haste":"Target yourself or an ally to become Hastened. The creature has a +2 bonus to Armour Class, Advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws, its Movement Speed is doubled, and can take one additional Action per turn.",
  "Healing Radiance":"Heal yourself and all nearby allies. Regain the same amount the next turn.",
  "Heart of the Storm":"When you cast a Spell of Level 1 or higher that deals Lightning or Thunder damage, you cause a small, local storm. All enemies within 6 m take (Sorcerer Level / 2) Lightning or (Sorcerer Level / 2) Thunder.",
