  "Hellish Rebuke":"React to your next attacker with flames that deal 2d10 Fire damage. On a successful save, the target still takes half damage.",
  "Hex Warrior":"You gain proficiency with Medium Armour, Shields, and Martial Weapons Prof. You gain Bind Hexed Weapon, which lets you use your Charisma modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity when attacking with weapons that you are proficient with.",
  "Hexblade's Curse":"Curse a target. Your damage rolls against the target gain a bonus equal to your Proficiency bonus. The number you need to roll a Critical Hit while attacking the target is also reduced by 1. If the target dies, you regain Warlock level + Charisma modifier.",
  "Hide in Plain Sight":"Camouflage yourself with your environment to become Invisible and gain a +10 bonus on Stealth Checks, as long as you stand still.",
  "Hold Monster":"Hold Monster a creature. It can't move, act, or react. Attacks from within 3 m are always critical hits.",
  "Hold Person":"Hold a humanoid enemy still. They can't move, act, or react. Attacks from within 3 m are always Critical Hits. At the end of each turn, the affected creature can make a WIS Saving Throw to end this condition.",
  "Holy Rebuke":"Call upon your Oath to grant a vengeful aura that deals 1d4 Radiant damage to anyone who hits them with a melee attack.",
  "Hound of Ill Omen":"Summon forth a creature of darkness.",
  "Hunter's Mark":"Mark a creature as your quarry to deal an additional 1d6 Weapon damage whenever you hit it with a weapon attack. If the target dies before the spell ends, you can use Reapply Hunter's Mark to mark a new creature.",
  "Hypnotic Gaze":"Charmed and Incapacitated a creature. It cannot attack you. It cannot act. You can Maintain Hypnotic Gaze your Hypnotic Gaze each turn to extend its duration.",
  "Ice Storm":"Impel a storm of hail and ice to crash from the sky, covering the ground and striking all objects and creatures within range, dealing Bludgeoning and Cold damage. It also creates an Ice surface that lasts 2 turns.",
  "Illusion Savant":"Illusion School is a subclass of Wizard.",
  "Illusory Self":"Interpose an illusory duplicate of yourself between you and an attacker's strike, making them miss their attack. You must Short Rest to use this feature again.",
  "Improved Abjuration":"Each time you take a Short Rest, the intensity of your Arcane Ward increases by an amount equal to your wizard level.",
  "Improved Bardic Inspiration (d10)":"The bonus gained from Bardic Inspiration (class action) increases to d8+1d8.",
  "Improved Bardic Inspiration (d8)":"The bonus gained from Bardic Inspiration (class action) increases to d8+1d8.",
  "Improved Combat Superiority":"The size of your Superiority Die increases to a d10 d10",
  "Improved Critical Hit":"The number you need to roll a Critical Hit while attacking is reduced by 1. This effect can stack.",
  "Improved Divine Smite":"Your attacks are suffused with divine might. Melee weapon attacks deal an additional 1d8 Radiant damage.",
  "Improved Elemental Casting":"Your affinity with elemental ki deepens. Several of your offensive Four Elements features deal an additional dice of damage, your Clench of the North Wind can hold an additional creature, and your Embrace of the Inferno fires an extra ray. Chill of the Mountain damage increases to 2d10 Cold (from 1d10) Clench of the North Wind can hold a…",
  "Improved Extra Attack":"You can make two additional attacks after attacking with your main-hand weapon.",
  "Improved Minor Illusion":"You can cast Improved Minor Illusion as a bonus action.",
  "Improved Unarmoured Movement":"Your movement speed increases by 3 m while you are not wearing armour or using a shield.",
  "Improved Warding Flare":"When an enemy attacks an ally, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll, possibly causing their attack to miss.",
  "Improved Wild Strike":"You can make 2 additional Attack Rolls after making an Unarmed Strike while in an animal Wild Shape.",
  "Indomitable":"Whenever you fail a Saving Throw, you can roll again, using the new result instead.",
  "Inescapable Destruction":"Damage you deal ignores Resistance to Necrotic damage.",
  "Infiltration Expertise":"Adopt a new identity, changing your appearance.",
  "Inflict Wounds":"Putrefy a creature with Necrotic energy filling your hands.",
  "Inquisitor's Might":"You or an ally's weapon attacks deal an additional Charisma modifier Radiant damage and can Dazed enemies for 1 turn.",
  "Insect Plague":"Locusts attack everyone within range, make the area Difficult Terrain, and impose Disadvantage on Perception Checks.",
  "Instinctive Charm":"Charmed an enemy attacking you. They will attack a new target if possible as a Reaction.see notes",
  "Intimidating Presence":"Menace an enemy and instil a terrible Fearful within them. You can use Maintain Intimidating Presence to prolong the target's fear.",
  "Intoxicating Strike":"Hit a creature with your bare fists and possibly get them Drunk.",
  "Intoxicating Strike (Bonus Action)":"Hit a creature with your bare fists and possibly get them Drunk.",
  "Inured to Undeath":"You have steeped yourself so completely in death that you are Resistant to Necrotic damage, and moreover your hit point maximum cannot be reduced.",
  "Invoke Duplicity":"Distract your enemies with an illusion. Within 3 m, Attack rolls have Advantage for you and your allies. Both the attacker and the creature must be within 3 m of the illusion.",
  "Iron Mind":"You gain Proficiency in Wisdom and Intelligence Saving Throws.",
  "Jack of All Trades":"Your vast experiences make you more likely to succeed in any undertaking. Add half of your Proficiency Bonus (rounded down) to Ability Checks that you are not Proficient in.",
  "Ki Resonation: Blast":"Detonate the ki of a creature Resonating Ki with you, hitting the creature and all creatures other than party members and summoned creatures within 5 m of it. The resulting explosion causes any nearby creatures Resonating with you to also detonate.",
  "Ki Resonation: Punch":"Hit a creature with your bare fists, making the ki in its body Resonating Ki with yours. You can then make this ki explode with Ki Resonation: Blast.",
  "Ki Resonation: Punch (Bonus Action)":"Hit a creature with your bare fists, making the ki in its body Resonating Ki with yours. You can then make this ki explode with Ki Resonation: Blast.",
